From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Bergin <peter.bergin@1x.tech>
Date: Mon, 9 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable nanobind strip-on-link for Yocto packaging

nanobind_add_module() unconditionally calls nanobind_strip() which adds
-Wl,-s as a target_link_option on the Python extension module. This
pre-strips the .so at link time, before Yocto's do_package step can
split debug symbols, causing a fatal "already-stripped" QA error.

Pass NOSTRIP to prevent nanobind from adding -Wl,-s. Yocto's packaging
step handles stripping via PACKAGE_STRIP_FLAGS.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE packaging specific]
Signed-off-by: Peter Bergin <peter.bergin@1x.tech>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -460,7 +460,7 @@
   # Configure nanobind: https://nanobind.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api_cmake.html
   nanobind_add_module(
     onnx_cpp2py_export
-    NB_STATIC NB_DOMAIN onnx STABLE_ABI FREE_THREADED LTO
+    NB_STATIC NB_DOMAIN onnx STABLE_ABI FREE_THREADED LTO NOSTRIP
     "${ONNX_ROOT}/onnx/cpp2py_export.cc" ${ONNX_SRCS} ${ONNX_PROTO_SRCS})
   add_dependencies(onnx_cpp2py_export onnx)
 endif()
